cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "Computational Docking and ADMET Analysis of Phytochemicals Against Escherichia coli DNA Gyrase B (PDB ID: 5L3J)"

message: "If you use this repository in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Ali"
    given-names: "Rehan"
    affiliation: "Department of Allied Health and Molecular Sciences, Lahore Garrison University, Lahore, Pakistan"

repository-code: "https://github.com/rehanaly/Computational-docking-and-ADMET-analysis-of-phytochemicals-against-E.-coli-DNA-gyrase-B"

abstract: >
  This repository presents a computational drug discovery workflow
  investigating the interaction of four phytochemicals (Berberine,
  Quercetin, Curcumin, and Resveratrol) with Escherichia coli DNA
  gyrase B (PDB ID: 5L3J). Molecular docking was performed using
  AutoDock Vina v1.2.7, followed by protein–ligand interaction
  analysis and ADMET prediction using pkCSM to identify potential
  antibacterial lead compounds.

